@startuml auth-flow

title API Auth Flow: Google OAuth + Sentinel JWT + Demo Mode

participant Browser
participant "API" as API
participant "Google Auth" as Google
database "TimescaleDB\n(users)" as DB

== Operator Login (Google OAuth) ==

Browser -> API : POST /auth/google\n{ id_token: "<google id token>" }
API -> Google : verifyIdToken(id_token)
Google --> API : { sub, email }
API -> DB : INSERT INTO users (google_sub, email)\nON CONFLICT (google_sub) DO UPDATE
DB --> API : user_id
API -> API : sign Sentinel JWT\n{ user_id, email, role: "operator", exp: now+24h }
API --> Browser : Set-Cookie: sentinel_jwt=...\nHttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict

== Demo Login ==

Browser -> API : POST /auth/demo
API -> API : IP rate limit check\n(1 token per IP per hour)
alt rate limit exceeded
    API --> Browser : 429 Too Many Requests
else within limit
    API -> API : concurrent demo WS cap check\n(10 active demo connections max)
    API -> API : sign Sentinel JWT\n{ user_id: "demo", email: "demo",\n  role: "demo", exp: now+3min }
    API --> Browser : Set-Cookie: sentinel_jwt=...\nHttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict
end

== Authenticated REST Request ==

Browser -> API : GET /alerts\nCookie: sentinel_jwt=...
API -> API : requireAuth: verify JWT signature + expiry\nextract user_id, role
alt operator or demo role
    API -> DB : SELECT * FROM alerts WHERE ...
    DB --> API : alert rows
    API --> Browser : 200 [ alert rows ]
else token missing or invalid
    API --> Browser : 401 Unauthorized
end

note over API
  requireOperator middleware rejects role: "demo".
  Applied to restricted routes (Phase 07 workspace,
  Phase 08 lifecycle, Phase 09 investigation).
  Standard read endpoints (alerts, entities/live)
  are accessible to both roles.
end note

== Authenticated WebSocket Upgrade ==

Browser -> API : HTTP Upgrade (WebSocket)\nCookie: sentinel_jwt=...
API -> API : verify JWT signature + expiry\nextract role, exp
alt token valid
    API -> API : store exp on socket object
    API --> Browser : 101 Switching Protocols
    API --> Browser : position updates / alert events (stream)
    note over API, Browser
      Demo sessions: server closes connection
      with code 4401 / "demo session expired"
      when wall-clock time reaches JWT exp.
      Operator sessions: no server-side close.
    end note
else token missing or invalid
    API --> Browser : 401 Unauthorized\n(upgrade rejected)
end

== Demo Session Expiry (WebSocket) ==

API -> Browser : close(4401, "demo session expired")
Browser -> Browser : show "Demo session ended.\nSign in with Google for full access." banner

@enduml
